{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00150",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 4.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. Where would you like me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.06,
      "end_seconds": 8.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.52,
      "end_seconds": 13.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Um, so... fever and chills. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.04,
      "end_seconds": 15.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.99,
      "end_seconds": 28.55,
      "duration_seconds": 11.56,
      "text": "Um, honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.48,
      "end_seconds": 33.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.25,
      "end_seconds": 58.18,
      "duration_seconds": 23.93,
      "text": "Honestly, a couple of times a week. I'd say severe. Oh, and sharp pain on the right side when I breathe in. That's been about the same, one week. As for sharp pain on the right side when I breathe in, a six out of ten, I suppose. I did have shortness of breath at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.37,
      "end_seconds": 61.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.78,
      "end_seconds": 63.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.23,
      "end_seconds": 81.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any vomiting or confusion at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.08,
      "end_seconds": 84.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.12,
      "end_seconds": 86.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Have you had any palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.12,
      "end_seconds": 90.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.93,
      "end_seconds": 96.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.88,
      "end_seconds": 110.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.3,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.77,
      "end_seconds": 114.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Right, what medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.79,
      "end_seconds": 127.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "It's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I'm, I'm on telmisartan, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.69,
      "end_seconds": 130.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.09,
      "end_seconds": 136.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "It's 40 milligrams. It's Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.55,
      "end_seconds": 141.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "I see. Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.76,
      "end_seconds": 144.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.06,
      "end_seconds": 151.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.39,
      "end_seconds": 157.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Pollen. I come out in... well, a runny nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.69,
      "end_seconds": 160.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.15,
      "end_seconds": 163.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.13,
      "end_seconds": 167.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.79,
      "end_seconds": 169.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.47,
      "end_seconds": 173.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.83,
      "end_seconds": 185.14,
      "duration_seconds": 10.31,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.29,
      "end_seconds": 189.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.69,
      "end_seconds": 190.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "I've got COPD."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.53,
      "end_seconds": 192.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.38,
      "end_seconds": 195.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.68,
      "end_seconds": 199.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.51,
      "end_seconds": 209.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "So, just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.42,
      "end_seconds": 237.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 22, saturation 89 percent, pulse 84, temperature is 36.9 degrees, blood pressure 136 over 90."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.92,
      "end_seconds": 240.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.97,
      "end_seconds": 248.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Alright, we'll put it in context in a moment. Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.85,
      "end_seconds": 253.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.82,
      "end_seconds": 267.6,
      "duration_seconds": 13.78,
      "text": "So, based on your history, I think we're dealing with a possible pneumonia on the right side at this stage. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out a pulmonary embolism yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.02,
      "end_seconds": 271.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.51,
      "end_seconds": 285.77,
      "duration_seconds": 13.26,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a possible pneumonia on the right side do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had fever and chills, severe, and no confusion or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.18,
      "end_seconds": 288.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.79,
      "end_seconds": 292.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.12,
      "end_seconds": 293.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.14,
      "end_seconds": 312.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let's get blood tests, for infection. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.48,
      "end_seconds": 314.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.77,
      "end_seconds": 334.88,
      "duration_seconds": 19.11,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray for suspected pneumonia. I'm prescribing levofloxacin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for five days. You take it by mouth. That should help with chest infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Rest and fluids, and finish every dose of the antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.43,
      "end_seconds": 351.23,
      "duration_seconds": 15.8,
      "text": "Mm. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. If the breathlessness worsens or you become drowsy, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.68,
      "end_seconds": 353.38,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.79,
      "end_seconds": 356.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Let's review you after the X-ray."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.99,
      "end_seconds": 358.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.89,
      "end_seconds": 364.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.75,
      "end_seconds": 375.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.71,
      "text": "So, uh, I take the levofloxacin, 500 milligrams, once a day and come back after the X-ray. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.47,
      "end_seconds": 381.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.77,
      "end_seconds": 384.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.54,
      "end_seconds": 386.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}